P8 Rust<->Python status leg + supervisor connection hardening (session 20)
===========================================================================
1) Python supervisor hardening (real defect from the live dev run in dev-1.log)
   ruke_ml/supervisor.py: a probe that hangs up mid-request printed a full
   ConnectionResetError traceback from socketserver. This process's stderr is the
   operator's only diagnostic channel, so noise there is a real defect.
   Mechanism: Handler.timeout = CONNECTION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S (15 s) so HTTP/1.1
   keep-alive cannot park a handler thread forever; Handler.handle_one_request and
   QuietServer.handle_error classify ConnectionError/TimeoutError as client churn
   (one log line) while every other exception still gets its traceback.
   Tests: tests/test_supervisor_workers.py RpcRoundTrip.test_h (RST mid-header and
   mid-body -> "connection closed by client", no "Traceback"), test_i (idle timeout
   bound), ConnectionOwnership (abort filtered, ZeroDivisionError still reported).
   Command: python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .   PY_EXIT=0
   Result: Ran 89 tests in 12.32s OK   (86 before; +3 tests)
   Also re-verified under the pinned uv venv (CPython 3.12.15).
