3) LIVE integrated proof (no inference involved - capability status only):
   python -m ruke_ml.supervisor --port 0 --discovery tmp-devcheck-data\python\mlstatus-test.json
   then ruke-server (RUKE_ML_DISCOVERY set, RUKE_BACKEND_PORT=3953):
     INFO ruke_server: capability backend rendezvous resolved
          endpoint=http://127.0.0.1:58079 source="discovery" supervisor_pid=Some(20544)
     GET /api/ruke/ml-status ->
       {"configured":true,"live":true,"source":"discovery","supervisor_pid":20544,
        "supervisor":{"state":"ready","active_jobs":0,"heavy_imports_at_startup":[],
                      "limits":{"heavy_concurrency":1,"idle_ttl_s":60.0,"mem_budget_mib":4096}},
        "capabilities":{... "status":"evaluation_required"|"not_configured" ...}}
   No token, no secret path and no audit line appears in the response or the log.
   Ownership fact learned: the venv python.exe re-execs the uv-managed interpreter,
   so the discovery record's pid differs from the launched pid. Teardown therefore
   uses THIS run's launched pid tree (taskkill /PID <launched> /T /F), never the
   record pid and never an image-name kill. After teardown: 0 ruke_ml python,
   0 ruke-server, port released.
